values ('ap_chemistry', 8, '8.4', array['8.4', '8.5']::text[], 'list_sequence', 'Weak acid + strong base: three cases', 'HA(aq) + OH−(aq) → A−(aq) + H2O(l) goes to completion; the pH method depends on which species remains.', '[{"label": "Weak acid in excess", "meaning": "Buffer forms; use the Henderson-Hasselbalch equation"}, {"label": "Strong base in excess", "meaning": "pH from moles of excess OH− and total volume"}, {"label": "Equimolar", "meaning": "Slightly basic; pH from A−(aq) + H2O(l) ⇌ HA(aq) + OH−(aq)"}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=task0067-chem-u5-u9-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_chemistry-u8-r1-017; ced=8.4.A.2 If the weak acid is in excess, then a buffer solution is formed')
