values ('ap_chemistry', 8, '8.11', array['8.11']::text[], 'convention', 'pH-sensitive solubility of salts', 'A salt''s solubility is pH sensitive when one of its ions is a weak acid, a weak base, or hydroxide, and the effect is explained qualitatively with Le Châtelier''s principle.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=task0067-chem-u5-u9-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_chemistry-u8-r1-034; ced=8.11.A.1 The solubility of a salt is pH sensitive when one of the constituent ions is a weak acid, a weak base, or the hydroxide ion')
